                <pb facs="0149" n="49" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg49"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.51/1036: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-28T16:00:00-00:44"><hi rendition="#italic">December 28,
                                1919—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 7:33 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Communicated Department’s December 10 [<hi rendition="#italic">20</hi>], 2 p.m.
                    to Liberian Government. In reply Legation advised that it is agreeable to
                    Liberian Government that National City Bank act as Fiscal Agent of Liberia for
                    advances which may be made the Republic from the United States Treasury and that
                    Liberian Government would be pleased to have Department approach bank on this
                    matter in its behalf.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
